  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 217 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nMuch Cooler End of Week:\n\nA much, much cooler airmass will move in behind the rain on \nFriday. The NBM has clearly trended toward the cold end of its \npreviously-large interquartile range over the past 24 hours, \nnow showing its mean high temperatures in the low to mid 60s on \nFriday and Saturday. Should this verify, those high temperatures\nwould be colder than most locations' minimum temperatures \ntonight. Furthermore, overnight low temperatures in the 30s will\nopen the door to a frost risk across portions of central \nMissouri and the eastern Ozarks Friday night and Saturday night.\n\nLooking ahead at ensembles for next week, however, shows that\nthese cooler temperatures may be short-lived as a building ridge\nbrings warmer air right back into the area on Sunday and Monday.",
